      ],
      "explanatory_notes": [
        "Changes how the shared gene network reads internal morphogen concentration. This chemical concentration includes local secretion, decay, and neighbor packet exchange; it is neither the target receptor stream nor a received spike trace.",
        "The is_M change alters a gene's response to the existing local motor-plane cue. It does not directly change the motor gain.",
        "These changes can alter growth and ongoing cell physiology. Without single-mutation or phenotype interventions, their separate contributions and behavioral mechanism remain unknown."
      ],
      "lateral_off_scope": "Suppresses in-plane spike ARRIVAL delivery after the fork; vertical spikes and morphogen PACKET exchange continue. Interaction measures the mutation's changed dependence on lateral spikes, which may be mediated by development."
    },
